ative play suggests saving my bomb unless I can win immediately or cripple the landlord’s last cards. Here, playing the bomb doesn’t secure victory and likely hands initiative back to the landlord after I lead weakly. Passing risks the landlord winning if my teammate can’t beat their last play, but it’s the better team play — my bomb would be more useful later if the landlord survives this round.  \n\n**Answer:**  \n{"cards": []}'}
